menu "Qoraal-flash"

config QORAAL_FLASH
    bool "Enable Qoraal-flash framework"
    default n

config QORAAL_FLASH_TALLIES
    bool "Enable persistent tallies (counters)"
    depends on QORAAL_FLASH
    default n
    help
      Per-module counters persisted to an application owned nvol3 volume.
      When disabled the TALLIES_* accessors compile to no-ops, so module
      source does not change.

config QORAAL_FLASH_TALLIES_PERSIST_INTERVAL
    int "Seconds between periodic tallie persists"
    depends on QORAAL_FLASH_TALLIES
    default 7200
    help
      How often the periodic pass writes dirty counters out.

      This is what bounds the history lost to a reset that cannot run code -
      a watchdog expiry, a brownout, the reset pin. The software reset paths
      halt the services on the way down and flush then, so they are not
      bounded by this.

      Shorter costs FLASH wear on a volume whose sectors are erased in place;
      longer costs history. Lower it while testing so that a periodic persist
      can be observed without waiting hours for one.

endmenu
